      "source": "https://www.visitwalkerville.com/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1904, Gordon McGregor launched the Ford Motor Company of Canada from his Walkerville Wagon Works.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitwalkerville.com/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hiram Walker’s factory workers lived in townhomes he built along Monmouth Road, still visible today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitwalkerville.com/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village’s name honors the Walker family, whose founder, Hiram Walker, began purchasing land in 1856 east of Windsor.",
